<title>MEXICO: Mexico's ICA starts up Venezuelan highway.</title>
<headline>Mexico's ICA starts up Venezuelan highway.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican construction giant Empresas ICA has started to operate a stretch of a Venezuelan highway between Caracas and La Guaira, a company director told reporters.</p>
<p>The director, requesting anonymity, said management of the 16.4 km stretch started up &quot;some days ago&quot; in line with ICA's concession which specified that operations were to begin from April this year.</p>
<p>ICA won the $220 million concession in the first half of 1995 for a period of 30 years. Part of the concession is to upgrade another 24-km stretch of the road and also a number of bridges.</p>
<p>((-- Monterrey bureau +528 3457617))</p>
